    "event": "Beach Hazards Statement",
    "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
    "senderName": "NWS Chicago IL",
    "headline": "Beach Hazards Statement issued September 14 at 9:22PM CDT until September 15 at 7:00AM CDT by NWS Chicago IL",
    "description": "* WHAT...High wave action and dangerous currents expected at Lake\nMichigan beaches. Waves 5 to 8 feet expected.\n\n* WHERE...Lake IL and Northern Cook Counties.\n\n* WHEN...Until 7 AM CDT Tuesday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Swimming conditions will be life threatening,\nespecially for inexperienced swimmers.",
    "instruction": "Remain out of the water to avoid dangerous swimming conditions\nand do not venture out onto piers, jetties, breakwalls, or other\nshoreline structures.",
